# Coil — Controls

This file fixes the actions a player drives the game with, the keys bound to
each, and what each one does on each screen. The screens themselves are in
`specs/ui.md`, and the turning rules a steering request obeys are in
`specs/movement.md`. Every figure below carries the name this specification gives
it.

## How input reaches the game

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
This game stands on no engine, so the keyboard belongs to the runtime layer you
write. What the game reads from that layer is one press edge per action per
frame, raised from the keys bound to that action. How the layer produces those
edges is yours to decide.
{{else if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
The keyboard belongs to the engine, which documents it in the `engine/` directory
at the root of this repository. The game registers the actions below with the
engine and reads one press edge per action per frame from it.
{{else}}
The keyboard belongs to the engine, which documents it in the `engine/` directory
at the root of this repository. The game registers the actions below with the
engine, and the player controller the game mode adds is the one place they are
read, one press edge per action per frame.
{{/if}}

Coil is keyboard only, and every action is a press edge. Holding a key does
nothing beyond the press that began it, and no action repeats while it is held.

## The actions

`ACTIONS` holds the actions the game registers, and `BINDINGS` maps each to the
keys that fire it. A key is named by its `KeyboardEvent.code`, so the bindings
hold whatever keyboard layout the player types on.

| Action | Keys |
| --- | --- |
| `up` | `ArrowUp`, `KeyW` |
| `down` | `ArrowDown`, `KeyS` |
| `left` | `ArrowLeft`, `KeyA` |
| `right` | `ArrowRight`, `KeyD` |
| `confirm` | `Enter`, `Space` |
| `back` | `Escape` |
| `pause` | `KeyP` |
| `mute` | `KeyM` |

The two sets bound to the four direction actions are interchangeable. `KeyW`
does exactly what `ArrowUp` does, wherever `up` is read.

## What each action does

An action's effect depends on the screen it is read on. `specs/ui.md` names the
screens and states which of them carry a menu.

| Action | On a menu-bearing screen | On `playing` |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `up` | Moves the highlight up one item, wrapping at the ends. | Requests a turn to `up`. |
| `down` | Moves the highlight down one item, wrapping at the ends. | Requests a turn to `down`. |
| `left` | Nothing. | Requests a turn to `left`. |
| `right` | Nothing. | Requests a turn to `right`. |
| `confirm` | Accepts the highlighted item. | Nothing. |
| `back` | Leaves the screen for the one it was reached from. | Pauses the round. |
| `pause` | Nothing, except on `paused`, where it resumes the round. | Pauses the round. |
| `mute` | Toggles sound. | Toggles sound. |

`mute` is read on every screen and does the same thing on each. `back` and
`pause` both pause a live round, so a player reaches the pause menu with either
`Escape` or `KeyP`.

A steering request is buffered rather than applied where it is read, and
`specs/movement.md` fixes the buffer, the tick that applies it, and which
requests are discarded.

## Out of scope

- Touch and gamepad input. The game is played from the keyboard alone.
- Rebinding. `BINDINGS` is fixed and the game offers no way to change it.
